From a5f06c09f8873ff50f4d90db39113dc7fb48beab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 10:59:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] mips: econet: externalize early boot and DRAM tooling

Move the EcoNet/Airoha MIPS early-boot implementation out of the U-Boot tree.

The standalone early-boot repository now owns DRAM calibration, BootROM
chainloaders, TCBoot/flash stages, bootext construction and their image tools.
Keep U-Boot focused on the proper second-stage image and the runtime SoC
initialization needed after the external DRAM/boot stage has completed.

Drop the duplicated DDR/flash/TPL/SPL/chainloader sources and host tooling,
remove their Kconfig and top-level Makefile hooks, and convert EN7580 back to a
plain U-Boot-proper target. Update the EcoNet board documentation and stale
DTS comments to describe the external early-boot boundary.

Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
