-payload is a build error; it must not be replaced by a fake external blob.
+The U-Boot tree produces the normal U-Boot artifacts such as ``u-boot.bin``,
+``u-boot.img`` and the configured device tree. Construct any board-specific
+``tcboot.bin`` or recovery/DRAMC image in the external early-boot repository.
 
 Current limitations
 -------------------
 
-* DDR initialization uses reconstructed assembly from the vendor calibration
-  objects, linked at ``0x9fa32800``. This is not a native, independently
-  documented DRAM driver. See ``tcboot-build.rst`` for provenance and limits.
-* The SFC implementation used by TPL and SPL is read-only. U-Boot proper uses
-  the Airoha EN7523 SPI-MEM driver with the EN751221 double chip-select quirk.
-  Flash erase/write must not be used until the board's BBT/BMT layout has been
-  verified.
-* Ethernet provides a polling-only U-Boot path through EN751221 QDMA0, GDM1
-  and the integrated MT7530. It deliberately preserves switch/PHY reset state
-  during chainloading. Cold-boot PHY initialization and multi-port control
-  still need board-specific validation.
-* U-Boot proper has been chainloaded and validated on physical hardware. The
-  complete BootROM -> TPL -> SPL -> U-Boot cold-boot path remains untested.
-
-TPL reports early failures with one character followed by a newline:
-``I`` for SFC initialization, ``F`` for DDR image reading, ``H`` for an
-invalid SPL header, ``S`` for SPL loading and ``L`` for a load address that
-cannot be reached through KSEG0/KSEG1.
+* The preceding DRAM stage must provide a valid ``REG_SAVE_INFO`` handoff.
+* U-Boot proper uses the Airoha EN7523 SPI-MEM driver with the EN751221 double
+  chip-select quirk. Verify the board BBT/BMT/ECC layout before modifying NAND.
+* Ethernet provides a polling U-Boot path through EN751221 QDMA0, GDM1 and the
+  integrated MT7530. Cold-boot PHY initialization remains board-specific.
+* U-Boot proper has been chainloaded and validated on physical hardware; the
+  reset-to-U-Boot path is owned and validated separately from this tree.
